<title>FRANCE: Paper firm Gascogne buys Papiethylene.</title>
<headline>Paper firm Gascogne buys Papiethylene.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>French paper company Gascogne said on Thursday that its Sopal subsidiary had purchased Papiethylene, a company which serves the building and agro-industry sectors and generated 85 million francs in 1996.</p>
<p>Gascogne chairman Philippe Blanc told a news conference the acquisition would place Sopal, which generates 1.2 billion francs in sales, in fourth place in packaging in Europe.</p>
</text>
